<article class="env-lemma" id="09YD">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09YD">Lemma <span data-tag="09YD">5.15.5</span>.</a> Let $U \subset X$ be a retrocompact open. Let $E \subset U$. If $E$ is constructible in $U$, then $E$ is constructible in $X$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Suppose that $V, W \subset U$ are retrocompact open in $U$. Then $V, W$ are retrocompact open in $X$ (Lemma <a href="/tag/005B" data-tag="005B">5.12.2</a>). Hence $V \cap (U \setminus W) = V \cap (X \setminus W)$ is constructible in $X$. We conclude since every constructible subset of $U$ is a finite union of subsets of the form $V \cap (U \setminus W)$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>